# The archive is DATA, and its line endings are load-bearing.
#
# Without this, git converts LF to CRLF on checkout under Windows. The archive's
# idempotency check compares whole lines to decide what is already recorded, so
# a stray carriage return makes every existing row look new — the appender would
# duplicate the entire file on the next run, on a Windows checkout only, and
# nothing about that failure announces itself.
#
# Committed data stays LF everywhere.
archive/**/*.csv text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything the build parses rather than a human edits.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
